TEXT 32 608 Left 2 !.param AMP=2 VOTHER=0 CLOAD=20p
TEXT 32 640 Left 2 !.param RF=330 CF=10n
TEXT 32 672 Left 2 !;.param RF=4.7k CF=1n
TEXT 32 704 Left 2 !.param RFX=mc(RF,0.01) CFX=mc(CF,0.05)
TEXT 32 736 Left 2 !.tran 0 3.3333m 0
TEXT 32 768 Left 2 !.meas TRAN glitch_pos MIN V(filt)-V(ref) FROM 416.667u TO 436.667u
TEXT 32 800 Left 2 !.meas TRAN glitch_neg MAX V(filt)-V(ref) FROM 1.25m TO 1.27m
TEXT 32 832 Left 2 !.meas TRAN err_rms RMS V(filt)-V(ref) FROM 0 TO 3.3333m
TEXT 32 864 Left 2 !.meas TRAN filt_rms RMS V(filt) FROM 0 TO 3.3333m
TEXT 32 896 Left 2 !.meas TRAN ref_rms RMS V(ref) FROM 0 TO 3.3333m
TEXT 32 928 Left 2 !.meas TRAN rms_err_ppm PARAM (filt_rms-ref_rms)/ref_rms*1e6
TEXT 32 960 Left 2 !.meas TRAN da_err_min MIN V(da)-V(ref) FROM 418.667u TO 833.333u
TEXT 32 1008 Left 2 ;SPICA sample: MUX507_2TO1 (+-5 V) switching an RC-filtered 3 kHz sine. EN toggles S1 <-> S0 every 416.7 us,
TEXT 32 1040 Left 2 ;so S0 connects at the +peak (416.7 us) and at the -peak (1.25 ms) of the sine: worst case for charge sharing.
TEXT 32 1072 Left 2 ;R1ref/C1ref = the same filter (same random R, C per run) without the mux. glitch_* = dip at connection, rms_err_ppm = error of the RMS value.
TEXT 32 1104 Left 2 ;CLOAD = everything on DA after the mux (buffer/ADC input + PCB): it usually matters more than the mux itself.
TEXT 32 1136 Left 2 ;Swap the .param lines to compare 330R/10n with 4.7k/1n. U1 carries the uniform Monte Carlo defaults (Ron, mismatch, caps, Qinj, timing);
TEXT 32 1168 Left 2 ;set e.g. RONK=1 CKS=1 CKD=1 QK=0 on U1 (SpiceLine) for a nominal part.
TEXT 32 1200 Left 2 ;No .tran max step is needed: the model has smooth gate edges, and 1 ns gives the same result ~130x slower.
